EXPECTED: NO_DOS_EFFECT

REASON: Netty 4.1.132.Final adds a per-stream CONTINUATION frame count limit that zero-length frames are charged against — assumption A1 is refuted

TARGET_IMAGE: eclipse-temurin:21-jre-jammy (custom Netty HTTP/2 server, netty-codec-http2:4.1.132.Final)
TARGET_PORT: 8443/tcp
CLIENT_TOOL: h2

DISPROOF_METHOD: assumption_refuted
DISPROOF_DETAIL: |
  Sent HEADERS with END_HEADERS=0 followed by zero-length CONTINUATION frames at
  maximum socket rate against a Netty 4.1.132.Final HTTP/2 server. The stream was
  reset with PROTOCOL_ERROR once the per-stream CONTINUATION frame count limit was
  reached. CPU stayed below 5% throughout. Memory delta negligible. The 1-byte
  payload pivot was also blocked by the same count-based limit. Static analysis of
  DefaultHttp2FrameReader in 4.1.132.Final confirms the count limit is independent
  of the byte check. Fix introduced in Netty 4.1.132.Final (CVE-2026-33871, March 2026).
DISPROOF_NOTES: Assumption A1 ("no count limit") is refuted. Netty 4.1.132.Final
                adds a CONTINUATION frame count limit that fires regardless of frame
                payload size, closing the zero-byte bypass of the byte-only check
                present in earlier versions.
